# C# style (tier 1)

## Quick rules

- Private fields: camelCase; types/methods/properties: PascalCase
- One primary type per file; file name matches type name
- Functions do one thing at one abstraction level
- Prefer explicit types over excessive var where clarity suffers
- Delete dead code; do not comment it out
- No static mutable globals in domain logic
- Interfaces at orchestration boundaries for replaceable implementations

## Audit focus

- Naming consistency
- Class size and responsibility scope
- Null handling at wiring boundaries
- Comment quality (explain why, not what)
